# MCP (Model Context Protocol) Integration System ✅

## Overview
The application now includes a complete MCP integration system that allows users to add custom MCP servers and seamlessly execute their tools alongside local tools. This system provides external tool discovery, execution, and management capabilities.

## Core Architecture

### MCP Integration Module
**Location**: [src-tauri/src/agent/tools/mcp_integration.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/mcp_integration.rs)

#### Key Components:
- **`MCPServerConfig`**: Configuration for MCP servers (command, args, environment, timeouts)
- **`MCPServerStatus`**: Connection state tracking (Disconnected, Connecting, Connected, Error, Timeout)
- **`MCPServerConnection`**: Individual server connection handler with STDIO JSON-RPC communication
- **`MCPManager`**: Central manager for all MCP server connections and tool execution

#### Core Functionality:
```rust
// Server lifecycle management
pub async fn add_server(&mut self, config: MCPServerConfig) -> Result<(), String>
pub async fn start_server(&mut self, server_id: &str) -> Result<(), String>
pub async fn stop_server(&mut self, server_id: &str) -> Result<(), String>

// Tool discovery and execution
pub async fn get_all_tools(&self) -> Vec<MCPToolInfo>
pub async fn execute_tool(&self, tool_name: &str, input: Value, call_id: String) -> Result<ToolResult, AgentError>
```

### Tool Configuration Extension
**Location**: [src-tauri/src/agent/tools/tool_config.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/tool_config.rs)

#### Enhanced Features:
- **`ToolConfig`** now includes `server_id` field for MCP tool association
